sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Platform User
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API Server<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant Operator as MCP Lifecycle Operator<br/>controller-runtime
    participant Deploy as MCP Server Deployment
    participant MCPPod as MCP Server Pod<br/>{spec.config.port}/TCP HTTP
    participant CM as ConfigMaps / Secrets

    Note over User,MCPPod: Flow 1: MCPServer Reconciliation

    User->>K8sAPI: kubectl apply MCPServer CR<br/>(mcp.x-k8s.io/v1alpha1)
    K8sAPI-->>Operator: Watch event (MCPServer created/updated)<br/>HTTP/2 long-poll, TLS 1.2+, SA Token

    Note over Operator: Phase 1: Validation
    Operator->>K8sAPI: GET ConfigMaps, Secrets<br/>HTTPS/443, SA Token
    K8sAPI-->>Operator: Referenced resources
    Operator->>Operator: Validate spec (image, port,<br/>container names, volume mounts)

    Note over Operator: Phase 2: Deployment
    Operator->>CM: Read ConfigMap/Secret data
    CM-->>Operator: Data for SHA-256 hash
    Operator->>Operator: Compute config-hash annotation
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Create/Update Deployment<br/>HTTPS/443, SA Token
    K8sAPI-->>Operator: Deployment status
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Check ownership & adoption

    Note over Operator: Phase 3: Service
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Create/Update ClusterIP Service<br/>HTTPS/443, SA Token
    K8sAPI-->>Operator: Service created

    Note over Operator: Phase 4: NetworkPolicy
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Create/Update NetworkPolicy<br/>HTTPS/443, SA Token
    K8sAPI-->>Operator: NetworkPolicy created

    Note over Operator,MCPPod: Flow 2: MCP Protocol Handshake

    Note over Operator: Wait for Deployment available replicas
    Operator->>MCPPod: MCP initialize request<br/>Streamable HTTP, {spec.config.port}/TCP
    MCPPod-->>Operator: MCP initialize response<br/>(capabilities: tools, resources,<br/>prompts, logging, completions)

    alt Handshake succeeds
        Operator->>K8sAPI: Update MCPServer status<br/>(Ready=True, capabilities)
    else Handshake fails (retry with backoff)
        Note over Operator: Exponential backoff:<br/>10s, 20s, 40s... up to 2min<br/>Max 10 retries
        Operator->>MCPPod: Retry MCP initialize
    else HTTP 401/403 response
        Note over Operator: Treat as reachable<br/>(server running, requires auth)
        Operator->>K8sAPI: Update MCPServer status<br/>(Ready=True, auth required)
    end

    Note over Operator,CM: Config Change Rolling Update

    CM->>K8sAPI: ConfigMap/Secret data changed
    K8sAPI-->>Operator: Watch event (field index)<br/>Re-reconcile triggered
    Operator->>Operator: Recompute config-hash
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Update Deployment<br/>(new annotation triggers rollout)
